; BFS hit-rate session: Workbench, a BFS volume and the counters of the handler.
; The assigns are the ones a normal startup makes. Without ENV: and T: commands
; such as List wait for a requester that nobody sees.
MakeDir >NIL: RAM:T RAM:Clipboards RAM:ENV RAM:ENV/Sys
Assign ENV: RAM:ENV
Assign T: RAM:T
Assign CLIPS: RAM:Clipboards
MakeDir >NIL: SYS:Prefs SYS:Prefs/Env-Archive
Assign ENVARC: SYS:Prefs/Env-Archive
Echo "BFS Hit-Rate-Sitzung: Zaehler auf 0 gesetzt."
C:hitrate BFS: RESET
Run >NIL: <NIL: Execute S:hitrate-loop
If EXISTS S:Autotest
  Execute S:Autotest
EndIf
If EXISTS S:Shellmode
  Echo "Shell-Modus ohne Workbench: Befehle hier eintippen (Dir, List, Copy, Delete)."
Else
  LoadWB
EndIf
